    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6850" root="حب" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُبَّةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُبٌّ</span>, in two places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَبِيبٌ</span>.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [It is also used in a pl. sense.] You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْ حُبَّةِ نَفْسِى</span> [<i>He is of the beloved of my soul</i>].
(TA voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُمَّةٌ</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُبَّتُكَ</span> also signifies <i>What
thou lovest to receive as a gift,</i> or <i>to have.</i> (K.)
You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِخْتَرْ حُبَّتَكَ</span> <i>Choose thou what,</i> or <i>whom,
thou lovest;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحَبَّتَكَ</span></b> . (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>A
grape-stone:</i> sometimes without teshdeed; (K;)
i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُبَةٌ</span>. (TA.)

